result_path = repo_root / "outputs/evaluations/pose_diagnostics_5fps/results.jsonl"
record = json.loads(result_path.read_text().splitlines()[-1])
print_pose_diagnostics(record)
```

## Plot Per-Horizon Errors

Each point measures the error at that exact future frame. It is not an average
from prediction step 1 through the displayed step. Solid lines are
autoregressive rollouts; dashed lines are teacher-forced predictions. A widening
gap between them identifies accumulated rollout error.
Each model uses the same seeded Gaussian draws in both modes so the comparison
does not change merely because a different random stream was sampled.

The plots cover trajectory displacement, transition velocity, pose scale,
orientation, heading, relative ordering, and body-frame keypoint error. P50
shows the typical paired case, while P99 exposes tail failures.

```python {"interpreter":"/home/splion/Desktop/personal/interpreting-social-navigation/.venv/bin/python"}
import json
import os
from pathlib import Path
import sys

from IPython.display import Image, display

repo_root = next(path for path in [Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents] if (path / "src").exists())
os.environ.setdefault("MPLCONFIGDIR", str(repo_root / "outputs/matplotlib"))
sys.path.insert(0, str(repo_root / "src"))

from diagnostics import save_horizon_profile_figure

result_dir = repo_root / "outputs/evaluations/pose_diagnostics_5fps"
record = json.loads((result_dir / "results.jsonl").read_text().splitlines()[-1])

for statistic in ("p50", "p99"):
    figure_path = save_horizon_profile_figure(
        record,
        result_dir / f"horizon_profile_{statistic}.png",
        statistic=statistic,
    )
    display(Image(filename=str(figure_path)))
```

## Inspect Worst Relative-Ordering Cases

```python {"interpreter":"/home/splion/Desktop/personal/interpreting-social-navigation/.venv/bin/python"}
import json
import os
from pathlib import Path
import sys

repo_root = next(path for path in [Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents] if (path / "src").exists())
os.environ.setdefault("MPLCONFIGDIR", str(repo_root / "outputs/matplotlib"))
sys.path.insert(0, str(repo_root / "src"))

case_path = repo_root / "outputs/evaluations/pose_diagnostics_5fps/cases.jsonl"
rows = [json.loads(line) for line in case_path.read_text().splitlines()]
single_rows = [
    row for row in rows
    if row["model"] == "single_mouse" and row["mode"] == "autoregressive"
]
single_rows = sorted(
    single_rows,
    key=lambda row: row["metrics"]["relative_ordering_error"],
    reverse=True,
)

for row in single_rows[:10]:
    print(
        row["sequence_id"],
        "start=", row["start_frame"],
        "mouse=", row["mouse_index"],
        "seed=", row["seed"],
        "motion=", row["motion_group"],
        "ROE=", round(row["metrics"]["relative_ordering_error"], 4),
        "BLE=", round(row["metrics"]["bone_length_error_px"], 3),
        "SOE=", round(row["metrics"]["skeleton_orientation_error_deg"], 3),
    )
```
